Regression tests using robot frameworks:

Prerequisites
Install Robot Framework and browser libraries:
pip install robotframework
pip install robotframework-browser
rfbrowser init # Only once, downloads browser binaries

File structure
tests/
  tinyflix_regression.robot
resources/
  TinyFlixKeywords.resource

*** Settings ***
Library         Browser
Suite Setup     Open TinyFlix
Suite Teardown   Close Browser

*** Variables ***
${APP_URL}      http://localhost:5173

*** Test Cases ***

Open Homepage And Verify Title
    Go To    ${APP_URL}
    Title Should Be    TinyFlix

Verify Search Functionality (Positive)
    Type Text    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    React
    Press Keys    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    Enter
    Wait For Elements State    .video-card    visible
    ${count}=    Get Element Count    .video-card
    Should Be True    ${count} > 0

Verify Search Functionality (Negative)
    Type Text    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    invalidsearchterm
    Press Keys    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    Enter
    Wait For Elements State    .video-card    hidden
    Page Should Contain    No videos found

Filter All Videos (Positive)
    Select Item From Dropdown
        Go To    ${APP_URL}
       Wait Until Element Is Visible    id=my-dropdown
      Select From List by Label    id=my-dropdown    Option 1
      Page Should Contain    Option 1
      [Teardown]    Close Browser
Filter All Videos (Negative)
       Go To    ${APP_URL}
       Wait Until Element Is Visible    id=my-dropdown
      Select From List by Label    id=my-dropdown    Option 1
     Click    text=InvalidCategory
    Page Should Contain    No videos found

Sort Videos By Title
    Click    text=Sort by Title
    Click    text=Popular
    Wait For Elements State    .video-card    visible
    ${title}=    Get Text    .video-card >> nth=0 >> css=h3
    Should Not Be Empty    ${title}

Edge Case: No Search Results
    Type Text    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    asdfghjkl
    Press Keys    input[placeholder="Search videos, tags, or descriptions"]    Enter
    Wait For Elements State    .video-card    hidden
    Page Should Contain    No videos found

Error Scenario: Invalid Page
    Go To    ${APP_URL}/non-existent-page
    Wait For Elements State    body    visible
    Page Should Contain    404

Accessibility Check: Tab Navigation
    Go To    ${APP_URL}
    Press Keys    body    Tab
    Press Keys    body    Tab
    Press Keys    body    Tab
    # Add further assertions if focus is visible

Critical Flow: Open Video Details (Positive)
    Click    .video-card >> nth=0
    Wait For Elements State    h1    visible
    ${heading}=    Get Text    h1
    Should Not Be Empty    ${heading}

Critical Flow: Open Video Details (Negative)
    Go To    ${APP_URL}/video/invalid-id
    Wait For Elements State    body    visible
    Page Should Contain    Video not found


TinyFlixKeywords.resource (Optional Keyword File)
*** Keywords ***
Open TinyFlix
    New Browser    headless=False
    New Context
    New Page    ${APP_URL}


How to Run the Tests
From the terminal:
robot tests/tinyflix_regression.robot


